WEBVTT

00:00:06.951 --> 00:00:36.299
Chapter 1 my first home.

00:00:36.319 --> 00:00:43.382
I live in a big meadow with a pond and trees around it.

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:50.746
During the day I run in the meadow with my mother and at night I sleep next to her.

00:00:50.806 --> 00:00:54.218
There are six other cults in the meadow.

00:00:54.278 --> 00:00:58.460
I run with them too and have great fun.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:02.362
But sometimes they kick and bite me.

00:01:02.422 --> 00:01:09.482
My mother always says These coats are good, but they're not polite.

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:13.946
You come from a family of famous horses.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:21.374
You must always be good and gentle, and never bite or kick.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:27.506
My mother's name is Duchess, and she is old and wise.

00:01:27.566 --> 00:01:35.448
She is our master's favorite horse, and she always takes him to town in a small carriage.

00:01:35.508 --> 00:01:38.730
Our master is a kind man.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:45.584
He gives us a lot of oats, a big carrot, and a warm place to live.

00:01:45.645 --> 00:01:49.408
He always says nice things to us.

00:01:49.468 --> 00:01:52.920
Sometimes he gives us some sugar.

00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.782
We all love him.

00:01:55.842 --> 00:02:04.479
One day, I see a lot of dogs running in another green meadow, and they are barking loudly.

00:02:04.538 --> 00:02:06.600
What's happening, mother?

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.872
I ask.

00:02:07.932 --> 00:02:11.194
The dogs are running after a hair.

00:02:11.254 --> 00:02:14.136
She says, there is a hunt.

00:02:14.196 --> 00:02:18.860
The dogs run fast, and the hair does, too.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.322
There is a lot of noise.

00:02:21.382 --> 00:02:26.754
Finally the dogs catch the poor hair and kill it.

00:02:26.814 --> 00:02:30.756
Then another sad thing happens.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:35.698
Two horses and two men fall to the ground.

00:02:35.758 --> 00:02:40.590
One man gets up, but the other does not.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:47.908
The dogs are silent now, and everyone is looking at the man and the two horses.

00:02:47.968 --> 00:02:53.025
It's young George Gordon, the landowner's son.

00:02:53.084 --> 00:02:55.225
Says mother, sadly.

00:02:55.285 --> 00:02:58.676
The poor young man is dead.

00:02:58.736 --> 00:03:05.679
Only one horse gets up, but the other cannot because his leg is broken.

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:10.490
Someone runs to the master's house and gets a gun.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:16.421
There is a loud shot, and the horse is dead.

00:03:16.481 --> 00:03:22.624
I am four years old now, and I am a handsome cult.

00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:28.688
I have a nice black coat and a white star on my forehead.

00:03:28.748 --> 00:03:34.211
One day, the landowner, Mr. Gordon, comes to look at me.

00:03:34.271 --> 00:03:39.754
He looks at my eyes, my teeth, and my legs.

00:03:39.814 --> 00:03:46.468
When you break him in, I want to see him, says Mr. Gordon.

00:03:46.528 --> 00:03:48.618
Very well, Mr. Gordon.

00:03:48.678 --> 00:03:50.480
Says my master.

00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:56.224
He smiles at me and says, Tomorrow, I must break you in.

00:03:56.244 --> 00:04:04.960
I must teach you to wear a saddle and bridle and carry a person on your back.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:10.324
Then I must teach you to pull a carriage.

00:04:10.384 --> 00:04:16.958
Tomorrow is an important day, says Mother quietly.

00:04:17.018 --> 00:04:25.404
Remember, you must always listen to your master and never bite or kick.

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:32.090
And you must never jump when you're happy or stop when you're tired.

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:36.244
Always be a good horse.

00:04:36.304 --> 00:04:41.969
The next day, my master comes and talks to me quietly.

00:04:42.029 --> 00:04:49.233
Then he gently puts the bit into my mouth and the bridle on my face.

00:04:49.293 --> 00:04:59.228
The bit hurts my mouth and feels terrible, but my mother and other adult horses wear it too.

00:04:59.288 --> 00:05:06.520
Then my master puts a saddle on my back and says kind words to me.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:12.833
He slowly gets on the saddle and rides me around the meadow.

00:05:12.893 --> 00:05:16.544
I am happy when I carry him.

00:05:16.604 --> 00:05:21.126
After some time, he takes me to the blacksmith.

00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:24.879
The blacksmith puts on horse shoes.

00:05:24.938 --> 00:05:30.972
They are very heavy metal shoes, and I do not like them.

00:05:31.032 --> 00:05:37.415
Today, we're going to visit my friend Simon, my master says.

00:05:37.474 --> 00:05:43.334
At Simon's house, I stay in a meadow with cows and sheep.

00:05:43.394 --> 00:05:50.653
Suddenly a big train goes by and it makes a lot of noise and smoke.

00:05:50.713 --> 00:06:00.556
I run to the other side of the meadow because I am afraid, but the cows and sheep do not move.

00:06:00.616 --> 00:06:08.548
A lot of trains go by, but they do not hurt me, so I am not afraid of them.

00:06:08.608 --> 00:06:12.851
Sometimes I pull the carriage with my mother.

00:06:12.911 --> 00:06:16.404
And she teaches me a lot of things.

00:06:16.464 --> 00:06:21.788
There are many kinds of masters, she says.

00:06:21.847 --> 00:06:27.380
Some are good, but others are bad and cruel.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:35.234
You must always listen to them and remember the good name of your family.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:41.485
In May, one of Mr. Gordon's men comes and takes me away.

00:06:41.545 --> 00:06:45.905
My master says, goodbye, my friend.

00:06:45.965 --> 00:06:50.888
Be a good horse and always do your best.

00:06:50.948 --> 00:06:57.474
I cannot say goodbye, so I put my nose in his hand.

00:06:57.534 --> 00:07:02.137
My new home at Mr. Gordon's is lovely.

00:07:02.197 --> 00:07:08.152
There is a big stable, and I have a comfortable stall.

00:07:08.212 --> 00:07:12.332
There is another horse in the next stall.

00:07:12.392 --> 00:07:15.502
Hello, what's your name?

00:07:15.562 --> 00:07:16.753
I ask.

00:07:16.813 --> 00:07:20.176
My name is Mary Legs.

00:07:20.236 --> 00:07:21.857
Says the horse.

00:07:21.916 --> 00:07:26.040
I carry the young ladies on my back.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.482
Are you my new neighbor?

00:07:28.542 --> 00:07:30.394
Yes, I am.

00:07:30.453 --> 00:07:32.716
Do you bite?

00:07:32.775 --> 00:07:34.906
Asks Mary Legs.

00:07:34.966 --> 00:07:37.138
No, I don't.

00:07:37.198 --> 00:07:38.440
I answer.

00:07:38.499 --> 00:07:41.222
I only bite grass.

00:07:41.282 --> 00:07:42.874
Oh, good.

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:49.489
Because the horse and the other stole sometimes bites, says Maryleggs.

00:07:49.549 --> 00:07:56.134
She's a brown horse, and her name is Ginger.

00:07:56.194 --> 00:08:09.173
Chapter 2 The Bridge My coachman's name is John Manley, and he lives near the stables.

00:08:09.233 --> 00:08:15.656
John is a friendly man, and he always gives me a good grooming.

00:08:15.716 --> 00:08:18.877
He is a good writer, too.

00:08:18.937 --> 00:08:21.198
Good morning, John.

00:08:21.258 --> 00:08:22.968
Says Mr. Gordon.

00:08:23.028 --> 00:08:25.559
How's the new horse?

00:08:25.619 --> 00:08:28.780
He's fast and easy to ride, sir.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.140
Says John.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.990
He comes from a good family.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.531
What's his name?

00:08:34.591 --> 00:08:36.311
Asks Mr. Gordon.

00:08:36.371 --> 00:08:38.172
I don't know, sir.

00:08:38.232 --> 00:08:39.462
Says John.

00:08:39.522 --> 00:08:43.634
Well, he's a beauty, says Mr. Gordon.

00:08:43.694 --> 00:08:47.826
Let's call him Black Beauty.

00:08:47.886 --> 00:08:52.530
I like my new name and my new master.

00:08:52.589 --> 00:09:00.514
After a few days, John says to me, Today you're going out on a carriage with Ginger.

00:09:00.574 --> 00:09:06.342
I am not happy about this because Ginger is not friendly.

00:09:06.402 --> 00:09:11.800
But after a few rides in the carriage, we start talking.

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:17.154
Sometimes I bite and kick, but I'm not a bad horse.

00:09:17.214 --> 00:09:19.606
Says Ginger, sadly.

00:09:19.666 --> 00:09:24.360
In my life, I can only remember crawlmasters.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:27.652
Bad Coachman, and the wick.

00:09:27.712 --> 00:09:32.096
Oh, I'm sorry Ginger, I say.

00:09:32.156 --> 00:09:34.498
Are you happy here?

00:09:34.558 --> 00:09:38.380
Yes, I am, says Ginger.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.892
Because the master and the coachmen are both kind.

00:09:42.952 --> 00:09:45.925
They understand horses.

00:09:45.984 --> 00:09:51.388
Now we are good friends, and I like her a lot.

00:09:51.448 --> 00:09:57.593
I also like merry legs, because he is always happy and friendly.

00:09:57.653 --> 00:10:02.422
He is the favorite horse of Miss Jessie and Flora.

00:10:02.482 --> 00:10:06.118
They are Mr. Gordon's daughters.

00:10:06.178 --> 00:10:15.480
One cloudy autumn day, the master says, John, get the carriage ready with black beauty.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:19.310
We must go to town on business.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:25.502
This is the first time for me to go to town with the master and John.

00:10:25.562 --> 00:10:27.642
I am excited.

00:10:27.702 --> 00:10:32.615
I want to do my best and please the master.

00:10:32.675 --> 00:10:41.272
The Master and John are in the carriage and it starts raining and it is very windy.

00:10:41.332 --> 00:10:46.704
We get to town and the Master goes to see some people.

00:10:46.764 --> 00:10:50.866
John and I wait for him in the rain.

00:10:50.926 --> 00:10:57.090
When he finishes his business he says, Let's go home John.

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:01.808
Perhaps we can cross the bridge before it is dark.

00:11:01.868 --> 00:11:06.887
It's a dangerous bridge when it rains, says John.

00:11:06.947 --> 00:11:12.900
We take the country road to the bridge and it is raining hard.

00:11:12.959 --> 00:11:17.441
I am very careful because the road is bad.

00:11:17.501 --> 00:11:22.833
When my feet touch the bridge, I know something is wrong.

00:11:22.893 --> 00:11:26.584
I cannot move and I stop.

00:11:26.644 --> 00:11:28.676
Go on, Black Beauty.

00:11:28.736 --> 00:11:30.398
Says my master.

00:11:30.458 --> 00:11:35.783
I cannot move because I feel there is danger on the bridge.

00:11:35.843 --> 00:11:39.826
There's something wrong, sir, says John.

00:11:39.886 --> 00:11:43.488
Beauty doesn't want to cross the bridge.

00:11:43.548 --> 00:11:46.310
But we must cross the bridge.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:49.652
It's late, says the master.

00:11:49.712 --> 00:11:56.156
At that moment, a man runs out of his house and cries, stop!

00:11:56.216 --> 00:11:57.178
Stop!

00:11:57.238 --> 00:11:58.416
Go back!

00:11:58.476 --> 00:12:00.536
Don't cross the bridge!

00:12:00.596 --> 00:12:02.658
It's broken in the middle!

00:12:02.718 --> 00:12:04.559
Broken in the middle?

00:12:04.619 --> 00:12:06.260
Says the master.

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:09.382
Oh, thank you, Black Beauty.

00:12:09.442 --> 00:12:12.756
Yes, thank you, Beauty.

00:12:12.816 --> 00:12:14.527
Says John.

00:12:14.587 --> 00:12:19.752
We take another country road and get home late.

00:12:19.812 --> 00:12:22.354
What a rainy night!

00:12:22.414 --> 00:12:25.336
Says the mistress when she sees us.

00:12:25.397 --> 00:12:27.926
I'm happy you're home.

00:12:27.986 --> 00:12:30.744
You can thank Black Beauty.

00:12:30.804 --> 00:12:33.886
He's a very wise horse.

00:12:33.946 --> 00:12:35.898
Says the Master.

00:12:35.958 --> 00:12:43.682
That night John dries my wet coat and puts on my warm blue blanket.

00:12:43.742 --> 00:12:49.716
Then he gives me a good dinner and I can finally sleep.

00:12:49.776 --> 00:12:54.648
The next day a new stable boy comes to work.

00:12:54.708 --> 00:12:57.416
His name is Joe Green.

00:12:57.476 --> 00:13:00.524
and he is fourteen years old.

00:13:00.584 --> 00:13:07.038
I like him because he has a gentle hand and he talks to me.

00:13:07.098 --> 00:13:13.872
One night the stable bell rings loudly and all the horses wake up.

00:13:13.932 --> 00:13:16.082
I hear John's voice.

00:13:16.142 --> 00:13:17.213
Beauty!

00:13:17.273 --> 00:13:18.364
Wake up!

00:13:18.424 --> 00:13:23.676
The mistress is very ill and we must go and find Dr White.

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:28.219
He puts a saddle on my back and gets on.

00:13:28.278 --> 00:13:32.900
I gallop fast because I want to help the mistress.

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:36.432
It is a dark, cold night.

00:13:36.492 --> 00:13:41.243
When we get to Dr. White's house, John calls him.

00:13:41.303 --> 00:13:52.311
A window opens and the doctor puts his head out and says, What's the matter at three o'clock in the morning?

00:13:52.371 --> 00:13:56.736
Mrs. Gordon is very ill, says John.

00:13:56.796 --> 00:13:59.758
Please come at once.

00:13:59.818 --> 00:14:03.160
Can I use your horse?

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.190
asks the doctor.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:09.252
My horse has a bad leg.

00:14:09.312 --> 00:14:13.244
Yes, of course, says John.

00:14:13.304 --> 00:14:18.506
The doctor is a heavy man and not a good rider.

00:14:18.566 --> 00:14:22.244
But I do my best and gallop home.

00:14:22.304 --> 00:14:27.430
He runs to see the mistress and Joe takes me to the stable.

00:14:27.490 --> 00:14:30.782
I am very wet and cold.

00:14:30.842 --> 00:14:35.594
Joe drives me and gives me some water and oats.

00:14:35.654 --> 00:14:40.205
But he forgets to put my warm blue blanket on.

00:14:40.265 --> 00:14:45.837
Soon I start shaking and I am very cold.

00:14:45.897 --> 00:14:49.054
I feel terrible.

00:14:49.114 --> 00:14:53.662
The next day, the Master comes to see me.

00:14:53.722 --> 00:14:59.336
Thanks to you, Black Beauty, the Mistress is feeling better.

00:14:59.396 --> 00:15:04.910
He says, but now you are ill, my poor Beauty.

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:08.412
We must call the vet at once.

00:15:08.472 --> 00:15:17.958
I am very ill now, but the Master's kind words make me feel better.

00:15:18.018 --> 00:15:31.962
Chapter 3 Lord and Lady Wadsworth My life at Mr. Gordon's is happy, but things are changing.

00:15:32.022 --> 00:15:38.014
The mistress is ill, and the master is sad and worried.

00:15:38.074 --> 00:15:49.194
Dr. White comes here often and says, Mrs. Gordon must go to warm country for two or three years.

00:15:49.254 --> 00:15:52.881
Then perhaps she can get better.

00:15:52.941 --> 00:15:58.472
Everyone is sad, because we must soon say goodbye.

00:15:58.532 --> 00:16:03.203
One day, Jesse and Flora come to the stable.

00:16:03.263 --> 00:16:05.553
Goodbye, dear Mary-Lax.

00:16:05.613 --> 00:16:06.924
They say.

00:16:06.984 --> 00:16:10.514
Thank you for all the wonderful rides.

00:16:10.574 --> 00:16:14.035
They hug him like an old friend.

00:16:14.095 --> 00:16:16.886
Don't be sad, Mary-Lax.

00:16:16.946 --> 00:16:18.396
Says Jesse.

00:16:18.456 --> 00:16:22.168
Father is selling you to the old vicar.

00:16:22.228 --> 00:16:26.970
He is a kind man and loves horses.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:33.495
Then the master comes to the stable and talks to Ginger and me.

00:16:33.555 --> 00:16:37.338
I'm selling you to Lord Wadsworth.

00:16:37.398 --> 00:16:41.190
He's a good man and lives in the country.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:44.552
Goodbye, Black Beauty and Ginger.

00:16:44.612 --> 00:16:48.656
He pats us on the neck for a long time.

00:16:48.716 --> 00:16:54.808
I cannot say goodbye, so I put my nose in his hand.

00:16:54.868 --> 00:17:01.040
Ginger and I are very sad to leave our master and our stable.

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:05.220
But this is the life of a horse.

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:12.612
Lord Wadsworth has a beautiful house with a green meadow and big stables.

00:17:12.672 --> 00:17:19.171
John and our new coachman, Mr. York, take us to our stalls.

00:17:19.232 --> 00:17:27.005
He looks at us carefully and says, They look like very good horses, Mr. Manley.

00:17:27.065 --> 00:17:29.616
What can you tell me about them?

00:17:29.676 --> 00:17:37.112
Black beauty is gentle and wise and always does his best, says John.

00:17:37.172 --> 00:17:40.184
He is also very fast.

00:17:40.244 --> 00:17:46.128
Ginger's a good horse too, but sometimes she's nervous.

00:17:46.188 --> 00:17:49.098
Do they wear the bearing rain?

00:17:49.158 --> 00:17:50.957
asks Mr. York.

00:17:51.017 --> 00:17:54.200
No, they don't, says John.

00:17:54.260 --> 00:17:56.732
Well, says Mr. York.

00:17:56.792 --> 00:17:59.134
Here, they must wear it.

00:17:59.194 --> 00:18:04.718
The Lord and I like a soft rain, but Lady Wadsworth wants the bearing rain.

00:18:04.778 --> 00:18:07.750
The horses must keep their heads high.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:12.334
Horses don't like it, says John.

00:18:12.394 --> 00:18:18.051
It's very uncomfortable, and it hurts their head and neck.

00:18:18.111 --> 00:18:20.735
You're right, says Mr. York.

00:18:20.795 --> 00:18:23.766
But the lady isn't kind.

00:18:23.826 --> 00:18:30.227
I do not know what a bearing rain is, but it sounds terrible.

00:18:30.287 --> 00:18:37.119
The next day Ginger and I pull the lady's carriage and we must wear it.

00:18:37.179 --> 00:18:42.700
It is very uncomfortable because we cannot put our heads down.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:46.233
It is a cruel thing for a horse.

00:18:46.293 --> 00:18:49.936
I hate the bearing rain.

00:18:49.996 --> 00:18:52.207
Says Ginger one evening.

00:18:52.267 --> 00:18:57.389
My head, neck and mouth hurt terribly.

00:18:57.449 --> 00:19:02.870
People don't wear it, so they can't understand.

00:19:02.931 --> 00:19:06.372
I hate it too, I say.

00:19:06.432 --> 00:19:09.633
But what can a poor horse do?

00:19:09.693 --> 00:19:12.834
We can do nothing, beauty.

00:19:12.894 --> 00:19:15.476
Says Ginger, sadly.

00:19:15.536 --> 00:19:19.489
We wear the bearing rain every day.

00:19:19.549 --> 00:19:34.213
The lady comes down the stairs in a beautiful dress and says, York, take me to the duchess of Boston, and I want the horse's heads high, very high.

00:19:34.273 --> 00:19:38.314
She gets into the carriage and sits down.

00:19:38.374 --> 00:19:41.605
York prepares Ginger and me.

00:19:41.665 --> 00:19:46.118
He comes to me first and pulls the bearing rain.

00:19:46.178 --> 00:19:48.512
It feels terrible.

00:19:48.572 --> 00:19:52.534
Then he goes to Ginger and does the same.

00:19:52.594 --> 00:19:57.286
Ginger gets angry and starts kicking wildly.

00:19:57.346 --> 00:20:03.179
York falls to the ground and the lady in the carriage screams.

00:20:03.239 --> 00:20:08.762
Two grooms come from the stable and take poor Ginger away.

00:20:08.822 --> 00:20:11.947
She does not ride with me anymore.

00:20:12.007 --> 00:20:16.933
The master uses her for the hunts because she is fast.

00:20:16.993 --> 00:20:23.817
My new carriage partner is Max, a quiet grey horse.

00:20:23.876 --> 00:20:27.408
I think about my old home a lot.

00:20:27.468 --> 00:20:34.371
Here I have food and a clean store, but I don't have a lot of friends.

00:20:34.431 --> 00:20:40.916
York is a good man, but he is not my friend.

00:20:40.976 --> 00:20:48.252
the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals.

00:20:48.312 --> 00:20:59.201
In the 1800s, animals are often mistreated by cruel owners and no one protects them.

00:20:59.261 --> 00:21:10.256
In 1824, Richard Martin opens the Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals in London.

00:21:10.317 --> 00:21:16.645
It is the first national animal protection society in the world.

00:21:16.705 --> 00:21:31.438
In 1840, Queen Victoria gives her permission to call it the Royal Society for the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals, the RSPCA.

00:21:31.498 --> 00:21:40.478
People begin to understand that animals are living creatures and it is wrong to mistreat them.

00:21:40.538 --> 00:21:50.462
Today, the RSPCA is an important organization with more than 400 inspectors.

00:21:50.522 --> 00:21:57.434
They visit homes, pet shops, farms and laboratories.

00:21:57.494 --> 00:22:02.866
They work with schools to teach kindness towards animals.

00:22:02.926 --> 00:22:09.493
They also work with the government to pass laws that protect animals.

00:22:09.553 --> 00:22:22.356
The RSPCA has animal hospitals and centres for abandoned animals, all over England and Wales.

00:22:22.416 --> 00:22:33.384
CHAPTER IV LISY Lady Anne is a friend of Lord Wadsworth's family.

00:22:33.444 --> 00:22:38.372
She is young and beautiful, and a perfect rider.

00:22:38.432 --> 00:22:43.196
I am her favorite horse and I like carrying her.

00:22:43.256 --> 00:22:48.438
She is kind to me and always brings me a carrot.

00:22:48.498 --> 00:22:52.818
She often rides with her friend, Lord Robert.

00:22:52.878 --> 00:22:57.380
He is a handsome young man with dark hair.

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:01.681
He likes horses and often talks to me.

00:23:01.741 --> 00:23:06.602
He rides Lizzy, a young, nervous horse.

00:23:06.663 --> 00:23:10.885
What a lovely spring day, says Lord Robert.

00:23:10.946 --> 00:23:13.477
Let's go riding, Lady Anne.

00:23:13.537 --> 00:23:15.628
All right, she says.

00:23:15.688 --> 00:23:19.131
But I want to ride your horse today.

00:23:19.191 --> 00:23:25.955
Liz is a good horse, but she's too nervous for a lady, says Lord Robert.

00:23:26.015 --> 00:23:29.038
What nonsense, says Lady Anne.

00:23:29.098 --> 00:23:35.083
Today I'm riding, Lizzie, and your riding black beauty.

00:23:35.143 --> 00:23:43.642
Lord Robert is a good writer, but I prefer Lady Anne because she is small and light.

00:23:43.702 --> 00:23:49.366
We gallop across the meadows and woods and have a wonderful time.

00:23:49.426 --> 00:23:53.230
Then we stop at Dr. Ashley's house.

00:23:53.290 --> 00:23:58.022
I must give a letter to the doctor, says Lord Robert.

00:23:58.082 --> 00:24:03.652
Lizzie and I can wait here with black beauty, says Lady Anne.

00:24:03.712 --> 00:24:07.760
After a few minutes, some cults run by.

00:24:07.820 --> 00:24:11.642
Lizzie is nervous, and she starts kicking.

00:24:11.702 --> 00:24:16.565
Lady Anne is afraid, and suddenly Lizzie gallops away.

00:24:16.585 --> 00:24:24.269
I know Lizzie is dangerous, so I nay loudly, and Lord Robert hears me.

00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:27.442
He runs to me and jumps on my back.

00:24:27.502 --> 00:24:28.972
Let's go, beauty.

00:24:29.032 --> 00:24:33.231
He cries, we must help Lady Anne.

00:24:33.292 --> 00:24:36.569
We follow Lizzie and Lady Anne.

00:24:36.630 --> 00:24:41.002
I gallop quickly because I want to help my mistress.

00:24:41.062 --> 00:24:45.845
Lizzie gallops up a hill and down into a valley.

00:24:45.905 --> 00:24:53.610
Lady Anne's green hat falls off and her long brown hair flies in the wind.

00:24:53.670 --> 00:24:59.392
Then Lizzie jumps across a small river and Lady Anne falls off.

00:24:59.452 --> 00:25:00.523
Oh no!

00:25:00.583 --> 00:25:02.350
cries Lord Robert.

00:25:02.410 --> 00:25:07.468
I jump across the river and see my poor mistress on the grass.

00:25:07.528 --> 00:25:11.420
Her face is white and her eyes are shut.

00:25:11.480 --> 00:25:14.421
She does not move or speak.

00:25:14.481 --> 00:25:17.162
Is she dead?

00:25:17.222 --> 00:25:22.304
Lady Anne, can you hear me?

00:25:22.364 --> 00:25:26.966
asks Lord Robert, but she does not answer.

00:25:27.026 --> 00:25:34.175
A young farmer is walking by and says, to poor lady, Can I help her?

00:25:34.235 --> 00:25:36.597
Yes, says Lord Robert.

00:25:36.657 --> 00:25:41.901
Please go to the village and come back with the doctor.

00:25:41.961 --> 00:25:44.493
You can ride my horse beauty.

00:25:44.553 --> 00:25:46.885
He's very fast.

00:25:46.945 --> 00:25:51.838
The farmer gets on my back and I gallop to the village.

00:25:51.898 --> 00:25:55.932
He finds a doctor and we return to Lady Anne.

00:25:55.992 --> 00:26:01.830
She is still on the grass and the doctor examines her carefully.

00:26:01.890 --> 00:26:06.484
Don't worry, she's not dead, he says.

00:26:06.544 --> 00:26:12.385
But we must take her home right now, and she must rest.

00:26:12.445 --> 00:26:18.276
I feel happy when I hear this, because I like my young mistress.

00:26:18.336 --> 00:26:24.387
That evening, in the stable, Ginger and I talk about Lizzie.

00:26:24.447 --> 00:26:34.894
Two days later, Lord Robert comes to my stall and says, Lady Anne is better now, and she wants to ride you soon.

00:26:34.954 --> 00:26:48.894
You are an intelligent horse beauty, because you understand a lot of things.

00:26:48.954 --> 00:26:56.300
When Mr. York goes to London, Ruben Smith becomes the coachman.

00:26:56.360 --> 00:27:01.666
He is a good, honest man, and he understands horses.

00:27:01.726 --> 00:27:05.788
But he has one big problem.

00:27:05.848 --> 00:27:10.330
He drinks a lot, and he is often drunk.

00:27:10.390 --> 00:27:17.913
One morning he comes to my stall and says, We're going to town on business beauty.

00:27:17.973 --> 00:27:21.565
He puts my saddle on, and we go.

00:27:21.625 --> 00:27:26.502
When we arrive in town, Smith leaves me at a stable.

00:27:26.562 --> 00:27:32.959
My horse is hungry and thirsty, says Smith to the stable boy.

00:27:33.019 --> 00:27:36.400
I'm coming back at four o'clock.

00:27:36.461 --> 00:27:42.142
The boy gives me oats and water and looks at my horseshoes too.

00:27:42.202 --> 00:27:47.094
The nails in your front show are loose, he says to me.

00:27:47.154 --> 00:27:50.285
You can't run with loose nails.

00:27:50.345 --> 00:27:52.996
I must tell Mr Smith.

00:27:53.056 --> 00:27:56.422
But Smith does not come at four o'clock.

00:27:56.482 --> 00:27:59.498
And he does not come at five o'clock.

00:27:59.558 --> 00:28:04.142
The boy is worried, and I am too.

00:28:04.202 --> 00:28:08.935
At nine o'clock in the evening, Smith comes back.

00:28:08.995 --> 00:28:12.557
He is angry, and his voice is loud.

00:28:12.617 --> 00:28:14.818
He cannot walk well.

00:28:14.878 --> 00:28:20.622
The fun shoe of your horse has loose nails, sir, says the boy.

00:28:20.683 --> 00:28:24.879
It's dangerous to ride a horse with loose nails.

00:28:24.939 --> 00:28:27.524
Smith looks at him and shouts.

00:28:27.584 --> 00:28:29.224
It's late.

00:28:29.284 --> 00:28:31.845
I'm going home.

00:28:31.905 --> 00:28:37.746
It is a dark night, and the moon is behind the clouds.

00:28:37.806 --> 00:28:41.528
Come on beauty, gallop!

00:28:41.588 --> 00:28:45.999
He cries and hits me with his whip.

00:28:46.019 --> 00:28:49.560
I gallop fast, but my front shoe is loose.

00:28:49.620 --> 00:28:51.830
I feel the whip again.

00:28:51.890 --> 00:28:53.972
Gala, bewy!

00:28:54.032 --> 00:28:56.104
cries Smith again.

00:28:56.164 --> 00:28:59.836
At the bridge my front shoe falls off.

00:28:59.896 --> 00:29:02.408
My foot hurts a lot.

00:29:02.469 --> 00:29:06.322
There are a lot of sharp stones on the road.

00:29:06.382 --> 00:29:09.894
I try to gallop, but I can't.

00:29:09.954 --> 00:29:15.768
At last I fall heavily on my knees, and Smith falls off.

00:29:15.828 --> 00:29:19.570
I get up slowly and look at Smith.

00:29:19.630 --> 00:29:22.059
He is not moving.

00:29:22.119 --> 00:29:24.120
What can I do?

00:29:24.180 --> 00:29:27.162
Soon I hear Ginger coming.

00:29:27.222 --> 00:29:30.654
I knail loudly and she answers.

00:29:30.714 --> 00:29:36.666
Then I hear men's voices and they stop in front of Smith.

00:29:36.726 --> 00:29:38.948
It's Ruben.

00:29:39.008 --> 00:29:40.308
Says one man.

00:29:40.328 --> 00:29:42.660
He's dead.

00:29:42.720 --> 00:29:44.150
Dead?

00:29:44.210 --> 00:29:45.901
Says another man.

00:29:45.961 --> 00:29:47.362
Yes.

00:29:47.422 --> 00:29:50.444
Says the first man sadly.

00:29:50.504 --> 00:29:53.478
Poor Ruben Smith.

00:29:53.538 --> 00:29:55.810
Look at his head.

00:29:55.870 --> 00:29:59.092
Then the man looks at me.

00:29:59.153 --> 00:30:02.434
Look at this poor horse.

00:30:02.494 --> 00:30:04.636
It's black beauty.

00:30:04.696 --> 00:30:07.759
His knees are badly hurt.

00:30:07.819 --> 00:30:14.014
The men slowly take me back to the stable, but I cannot sleep.

00:30:14.074 --> 00:30:18.300
The next day the vet and the blacksmith come to see me.

00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:23.035
Loose horse must rest for a few months," says the vet.

00:30:23.095 --> 00:30:28.646
So now I stay in the green meadow with its sweet grass.

00:30:28.706 --> 00:30:34.968
But I am worried about the future, because my knees are not perfect.

00:30:35.028 --> 00:30:41.859
After a month, Ginger comes to the meadow, too, because she is very tired.

00:30:41.919 --> 00:30:46.497
I like talking to my old friend under the apple tree.

00:30:46.557 --> 00:30:51.938
One summer day, Lord Wadsworth and York come to the meadow.

00:30:51.998 --> 00:30:54.780
They look at my knees.

00:30:54.840 --> 00:31:01.346
I'm sorry, York, but I must sell black beauty, says the Lord.

00:31:01.406 --> 00:31:04.878
His knees are not perfect anymore.

00:31:04.938 --> 00:31:09.721
I can't keep a horse with those knees in my stables.

00:31:09.782 --> 00:31:13.024
I'm very sorry because I like beauty.

00:31:13.084 --> 00:31:24.944
He's a wonderful horse, but his knees When they go away, Ginger says sadly, You're the only friend I've got.

00:31:25.004 --> 00:31:27.526
And soon you must leave.

00:31:27.586 --> 00:31:31.158
What a difficult life.

00:31:31.218 --> 00:31:38.733
I look at her and say, Ginger, you're my true friend.

00:31:38.794 --> 00:31:43.146
The Lord sells me to the town livery stables.

00:31:43.206 --> 00:31:45.768
It is not a nice place.

00:31:45.828 --> 00:31:50.980
Anyone can hire a horse and carriage at delivery stables.

00:31:51.040 --> 00:32:00.886
Most of the drivers are bad and know nothing about horses, and of course they know nothing about driving a carriage.

00:32:00.946 --> 00:32:07.330
They make a lot of mistakes and then get angry with the horse and use the whip.

00:32:07.390 --> 00:32:14.154
In the evening I cannot talk about my day because I do not know the other horses.

00:32:14.214 --> 00:32:20.828
I am very lonely and think about ginger.

00:32:20.888 --> 00:32:25.571
Listening activity.

00:32:25.631 --> 00:32:27.982
Good morning.

00:32:28.042 --> 00:32:30.584
Is this Jones's stables?

00:32:30.644 --> 00:32:31.796
Yes, sir.

00:32:31.856 --> 00:32:33.426
Can I help you?

00:32:33.486 --> 00:32:36.568
I'm in town on business today.

00:32:36.628 --> 00:32:39.000
Can I leave my horse here?

00:32:39.060 --> 00:32:41.082
Yes, of course.

00:32:41.142 --> 00:32:43.550
What time do you close?

00:32:43.610 --> 00:32:46.268
We close at 10pm.

00:32:46.328 --> 00:32:47.488
Good.

00:32:47.548 --> 00:32:51.010
I'm coming back at 4pm.

00:32:51.070 --> 00:32:54.822
My horse is hungry and thirsty.

00:32:54.882 --> 00:32:58.013
How much do oats and water cost?

00:32:58.073 --> 00:33:00.074
For pincer.

00:33:00.134 --> 00:33:03.405
I want to buy some new rains too.

00:33:03.465 --> 00:33:07.326
We have brown and black rains.

00:33:07.386 --> 00:33:08.337
Good.

00:33:08.397 --> 00:33:11.616
I want two black rains.

00:33:11.676 --> 00:33:14.046
Do you sell blankets, too?

00:33:14.106 --> 00:33:16.088
No, we don't, sir.

00:33:16.148 --> 00:33:19.190
Where can I buy a blanket for my horse?

00:33:19.250 --> 00:33:22.513
At Mr. Smith's shop near the town inn.

00:33:22.573 --> 00:33:24.514
Where's the town inn?

00:33:24.575 --> 00:33:26.876
It's behind the church.

00:33:26.936 --> 00:33:29.748
Thank you.

00:33:29.808 --> 00:33:43.408
Chapter 6 A London Cab Horse After a year at the livery stables, the master takes me to a horse-fair.

00:33:43.469 --> 00:33:45.731
He wants to sell me.

00:33:45.791 --> 00:33:49.454
A horse-fair is an interesting place.

00:33:49.514 --> 00:33:57.862
Some of the horses at the fair are young and handsome, but most of them are old and tired.

00:33:57.922 --> 00:34:03.011
Their eyes are sad and they are thin and hungry.

00:34:03.071 --> 00:34:09.127
I am still a strong horse, but my knees are not perfect anymore.

00:34:09.187 --> 00:34:13.118
People come to look at me, and they like me.

00:34:13.178 --> 00:34:17.440
But when they see my knees, they go away.

00:34:17.500 --> 00:34:23.252
At the end of the day, a tall, thin man comes and looks at me.

00:34:23.312 --> 00:34:25.583
Then he talks to my master.

00:34:25.603 --> 00:34:30.750
"'I'm looking for a gentle horse," he says.

00:34:30.810 --> 00:34:35.297
I want to ride him in the fresh air every morning.

00:34:35.358 --> 00:34:39.911
This black horse is perfect, says my master.

00:34:39.971 --> 00:34:42.042
He's very gentle.

00:34:42.102 --> 00:34:47.807
My new master is Mr. Barry, and he lives in Bath.

00:34:47.866 --> 00:34:53.250
He knows nothing about horses, but he is a kind man.

00:34:53.309 --> 00:34:59.835
He buys a lot of food, but the stable boy steals it and takes it home.

00:34:59.896 --> 00:35:03.308
He is dishonest and lazy.

00:35:03.368 --> 00:35:07.020
He never cleans my feet or my stool.

00:35:07.080 --> 00:35:10.883
Mr. Barry knows nothing about this.

00:35:10.943 --> 00:35:17.156
One day, Mr. Barry's friend says, Your horse is very thin.

00:35:17.216 --> 00:35:19.498
What's the matter with him?

00:35:19.558 --> 00:35:22.540
I don't know, says Mr. Barry.

00:35:22.600 --> 00:35:26.027
I always buy a lot of food for him.

00:35:26.087 --> 00:35:31.794
Go and see what's happening in the stable," says his friend.

00:35:31.854 --> 00:35:39.377
My master discovers that the stable boy steals my food and my stall is very dirty.

00:35:39.437 --> 00:35:43.058
He is angry and calls the police.

00:35:43.118 --> 00:35:47.250
They take the stable boy to prison for two months.

00:35:47.310 --> 00:35:52.801
Then Mr. Barry comes to my stall and looks at me sadly.

00:35:52.861 --> 00:35:55.806
I'm sorry, Beauty, he says.

00:35:55.866 --> 00:35:58.792
Let's sell you at the next horse fare.

00:35:58.852 --> 00:36:01.282
I'm not lucky with horses.

00:36:01.342 --> 00:36:07.186
I am sorry too, because I do not like changing masters.

00:36:07.246 --> 00:36:14.820
At the next horse fare, a short man with kind grey eyes comes to look at me.

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:18.642
He pats my neck gently and smiles.

00:36:18.703 --> 00:36:22.645
I like this horse, he says to the man.

00:36:22.705 --> 00:36:25.665
I can pay £24 for him.

00:36:25.725 --> 00:36:31.105
Harry, well, the horse is yours, says the man.

00:36:31.166 --> 00:36:36.128
My new master is a cab driver and lives in London.

00:36:36.188 --> 00:36:41.460
His name is Jerry Barker and his wife's name is Polly.

00:36:41.520 --> 00:36:45.942
They have got two children, Dolly and Harry.

00:36:46.002 --> 00:36:50.603
They are a very happy family and they like me.

00:36:50.664 --> 00:36:53.963
Captain is Jerry's other horse.

00:36:54.023 --> 00:36:58.824
He is a big, white horse, and he seems friendly.

00:36:58.884 --> 00:37:04.748
Our campstand is in the centre of London, and there are many horses.

00:37:04.808 --> 00:37:12.502
Jerry is an excellent driver, and he never uses the whip or the bearing-rain.

00:37:12.562 --> 00:37:17.295
Our stable is clean, and we are never hungry.

00:37:17.355 --> 00:37:21.149
I am lucky to have a kind master.

00:37:21.209 --> 00:37:28.296
Sunday is the best day because I can rest all day and talk to Captain.

00:37:28.357 --> 00:37:36.302
He is an old military horse and tells me exciting stories about different wars.

00:37:36.362 --> 00:37:40.646
The life of a cab horse is difficult.

00:37:40.706 --> 00:37:48.052
London is a big city with a lot of noise, people, carriages and cabs.

00:37:48.112 --> 00:37:51.802
The weather is often wet and cold.

00:37:51.862 --> 00:37:58.160
At the end of the day, I am very tired and my knees hurt.

00:37:58.220 --> 00:38:01.562
Captain has the same problem.

00:38:01.622 --> 00:38:07.114
In the winter, Dolly often brings her father a hot lunch.

00:38:07.174 --> 00:38:10.156
He eats it at the cab stand.

00:38:10.216 --> 00:38:13.598
Jerry's life is difficult too.

00:38:13.658 --> 00:38:17.940
One day, our cab is waiting outside a park.

00:38:18.000 --> 00:38:21.161
Another cab stops next to us.

00:38:21.222 --> 00:38:26.503
An old, tired brown horse is pulling the cab.

00:38:26.563 --> 00:38:33.444
The poor horse has a long, thin neck, and her eyes are almost shut.

00:38:33.504 --> 00:38:37.695
I can see her bones through her dirty coat.

00:38:37.755 --> 00:38:46.016
She looks at me with her sad eyes and says, Is that you, Black Beauty?

00:38:46.076 --> 00:38:51.400
Ginger, my old friend, I answer.

00:38:51.460 --> 00:38:56.334
Yes, it's me, Black Beauty.

00:38:56.394 --> 00:38:59.226
It's good to see you.

00:38:59.286 --> 00:39:00.848
Says Ginger.

00:39:00.908 --> 00:39:02.669
I feel terrible.

00:39:02.689 --> 00:39:09.372
I am old, weak, hungry, and ill.

00:39:09.432 --> 00:39:13.266
I can't run or gallop anymore.

00:39:13.326 --> 00:39:21.529
I must pull this heavy cab for my cruel master, and I eat very little.

00:39:21.589 --> 00:39:26.080
I work all week and never have a day of rest.

00:39:26.140 --> 00:39:31.172
Every bone in my old body hurts.

00:39:31.232 --> 00:39:34.294
How terrible.

00:39:34.354 --> 00:39:38.276
I put my nose near hers.

00:39:38.336 --> 00:39:43.769
Dear Ginger, I'm very sorry.

00:39:43.829 --> 00:39:50.162
A week later, I see a cart with a dead horse in it.

00:39:50.222 --> 00:39:52.748
It is Ginger.

00:39:52.808 --> 00:39:58.154
I feel very sad when I see her body in the cart.

00:39:58.214 --> 00:40:01.576
Why are people cruel to animals?

00:40:01.636 --> 00:40:04.298
They do not understand us.

00:40:04.359 --> 00:40:10.241
We only want some love and kindness.

00:40:10.302 --> 00:40:14.194
Horses.

00:40:14.254 --> 00:40:18.026
Horses are beautiful animals.

00:40:18.087 --> 00:40:21.583
They are intelligent and friendly.

00:40:21.643 --> 00:40:24.970
and they learn quickly too.

00:40:25.030 --> 00:40:31.516
Their favorite foods are oats, carrots and apples.

00:40:31.576 --> 00:40:34.538
They do not eat meat.

00:40:34.598 --> 00:40:38.540
Horses love conversation.

00:40:38.600 --> 00:40:44.386
You can talk to a horse and he listens to you happily.

00:40:44.446 --> 00:40:52.580
There are three types of horses, light, heavy, and ponies.

00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:57.192
Each kind of horse has a lot of breeds.

00:40:57.252 --> 00:41:06.109
Breeds are groups of horses with different colours and sizes.

00:41:06.129 --> 00:41:07.090
1.

00:41:07.150 --> 00:41:19.254
Light Horses They have small bones and thin legs, and they weigh about 650 kg.

00:41:19.314 --> 00:41:25.134
Saddlehorses are light horses.

00:41:25.194 --> 00:41:29.054
People use them for riding.

00:41:29.114 --> 00:41:42.796
Some important breeds of saddlehorses are thoroughbred horses, American saddlehorses and Arabian stallions.

00:41:42.857 --> 00:41:51.225
Quarterhorses, they are fast, strong and intelligent.

00:41:51.285 --> 00:41:55.952
They work well with other animals.

00:41:56.013 --> 00:41:59.653
Vipizana horses.

00:41:59.713 --> 00:42:04.154
They are beautiful show horses.

00:42:04.214 --> 00:42:09.645
They have a white coat and strong legs.

00:42:09.705 --> 00:42:17.656
These horses are part of the Spanish riding school in Vienna, Austria.

00:42:17.716 --> 00:42:21.578
It is a very famous riding school.

00:42:21.638 --> 00:42:28.653
You can visit it, and watch the lipids on a horse's dance to music.

00:42:28.713 --> 00:42:30.994
Two.

00:42:31.054 --> 00:42:33.796
Heavy horses.

00:42:33.856 --> 00:42:42.173
They have big bones and big legs, and they weigh around 1,300 kilograms.

00:42:42.213 --> 00:42:49.870
Draft horses are very tall, heavy and strong.

00:42:49.930 --> 00:42:57.959
People use them for heavy work and in shows.

00:42:58.019 --> 00:43:11.512
Some important breeds of draft horses are Clyde'sdale horses, Shire horses and Percheron horses.

00:43:11.572 --> 00:43:14.054
Three.

00:43:14.114 --> 00:43:16.204
Ponies.

00:43:16.264 --> 00:43:23.876
They are small, short horses and they weigh around 400 kilograms.

00:43:23.936 --> 00:43:26.546
Ponies are gentle.

00:43:26.606 --> 00:43:30.358
They are good horses for young riders.

00:43:30.418 --> 00:43:34.460
They are strong, clever animals.

00:43:34.520 --> 00:43:45.976
Some important breeds of ponies are Shetland ponies, Welsh ponies and Dartmoor ponies.

00:43:46.036 --> 00:43:50.101
Horses at work.

00:43:50.161 --> 00:43:58.126
Today, cars, buses, trains and airplanes take people everywhere.

00:43:58.187 --> 00:44:02.630
But horses are still part of our lives.

00:44:02.690 --> 00:44:06.862
We ride horses for fun and sport.

00:44:06.922 --> 00:44:10.616
We watch them perform at the circus.

00:44:10.676 --> 00:44:16.730
People go to the horse races and watch their favorite horse.

00:44:16.790 --> 00:44:24.177
Cowboys ride bucking Broncos at rodeos in the United States.

00:44:24.237 --> 00:44:31.904
Police men and police women ride horses in big cities like New York City.

00:44:31.964 --> 00:44:40.260
Cowboys in North American ranches ride quarter horses when they work with cattle.

00:44:40.321 --> 00:44:48.281
A ride in a horse and carriage is a big tourist attraction in some towns and cities.

00:44:48.341 --> 00:44:55.382
In poor countries, people use horses to work on farms and to travel.

00:44:55.442 --> 00:45:07.799
In some North European countries, horses and ponies pull slays in the snow.

00:45:07.859 --> 00:45:21.968
Christmas and New Year's Eve are happy times for some people but not for cab drivers and their horses.

00:45:22.028 --> 00:45:27.732
During that time we work hard and stay out late.

00:45:27.792 --> 00:45:35.871
Often we must wait for hours in the rain or snow while people are at parties.

00:45:35.931 --> 00:45:44.401
On New Year's Eve, Jerry and I take two gentlemen to a party in a big house.

00:45:44.461 --> 00:45:52.756
Come back for us at eleven o'clock and don't be late, says one of the gentlemen.

00:45:52.816 --> 00:46:00.651
At eleven o'clock we are in front of the big house, but the gentlemen are not there.

00:46:00.711 --> 00:46:06.250
It is a very cold night and it is snowing.

00:46:06.310 --> 00:46:11.711
The church bell says it's midnight, says Jerry.

00:46:11.771 --> 00:46:15.334
But the gentlemen are not here.

00:46:15.394 --> 00:46:19.568
We continue to wait in the cold.

00:46:19.629 --> 00:46:28.096
At a quarter past one, the door of the big house opens and the two gentlemen come out.

00:46:28.156 --> 00:46:34.126
They do not say a word to Jerry, and we take them home.

00:46:34.187 --> 00:46:40.474
When we get home, Jerry cannot speak and he coughs a lot.

00:46:40.534 --> 00:46:45.814
He dries me and puts a warm blanket on my back.

00:46:45.874 --> 00:46:51.526
The next morning, Harry comes to give me oats and water.

00:46:51.586 --> 00:46:57.798
He pats my neck gently and says, My father is very ill.

00:46:57.858 --> 00:47:00.838
He can't drive his cab anymore.

00:47:00.899 --> 00:47:03.728
He must find another job.

00:47:03.788 --> 00:47:08.012
We must sell you to another cab driver.

00:47:08.072 --> 00:47:12.436
I'm very sorry dear old friend.

00:47:12.496 --> 00:47:15.468
Dolly comes and kisses me.

00:47:15.528 --> 00:47:18.180
Then she starts crying.

00:47:18.241 --> 00:47:21.734
Goodbye old friend.

00:47:21.794 --> 00:47:27.018
I am very sad to leave Jerry and his family.

00:47:27.078 --> 00:47:31.400
My new master is Nicholas Skinner.

00:47:31.460 --> 00:47:37.872
He has black eyes and black hair, and a loud voice.

00:47:37.932 --> 00:47:42.454
He drives an old cab in a bad part of London.

00:47:42.514 --> 00:47:46.746
He often whips my back and my head.

00:47:46.806 --> 00:47:52.409
He is a cruel master, but I always do my best.

00:47:52.469 --> 00:47:59.167
I eat little and work twelve hours a day, seven days a week.

00:47:59.227 --> 00:48:04.346
There is no time to rest or to talk to other horses.

00:48:04.406 --> 00:48:08.879
My life is very unhappy.

00:48:08.939 --> 00:48:17.866
One morning we go to the railway station and pick up a lady, a man, a young girl and a little boy.

00:48:17.926 --> 00:48:21.018
They have a lot of heavy luggage.

00:48:21.078 --> 00:48:24.892
Skinner puts all the luggage in the cab.

00:48:24.952 --> 00:48:28.438
The young girl comes and looks at me.

00:48:28.498 --> 00:49:00.110
father she says this poor horse can't take us and all our luggage he is weak and thin please come and look at him what nonsense says the man get in the cab at once and be quiet i start to pull the heavy cab to ludgate hill then i try to climb the hill But I feel weak.

00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:03.761
Suddenly, I fall to the ground.

00:49:03.822 --> 00:49:05.952
I try to get up.

00:49:06.013 --> 00:49:07.634
But I cannot.

00:49:07.694 --> 00:49:11.596
How the poor horse cries the young girl.

00:49:11.656 --> 00:49:13.527
We are cruel.

00:49:13.587 --> 00:49:20.442
A young man throws some cold water on my head and I slowly get up.

00:49:20.502 --> 00:49:27.114
Skinner takes me back to the stables and says, you're working very hard.

00:49:27.174 --> 00:49:32.046
Rest for a week, and then I must sell you at the horse fair.

00:49:32.106 --> 00:49:35.858
You're not a good horse for my cab.

00:49:35.918 --> 00:49:44.895
The horses at the fair are old and tired, and the people are not rich gentlemen.

00:49:44.955 --> 00:49:46.956
They are farmers.

00:49:47.016 --> 00:49:51.580
A farmer and his grandson stop in front of me.

00:49:51.640 --> 00:49:54.031
Look at this horse, William.

00:49:54.091 --> 00:49:55.442
Says the farmer.

00:49:55.502 --> 00:49:59.615
He is tired and thin, but he is handsome.

00:49:59.675 --> 00:50:02.277
He comes from a good family.

00:50:02.337 --> 00:50:04.970
Look at his neck and ears.

00:50:05.030 --> 00:50:11.004
The young boy pats my face, and I put my nose in his hand.

00:50:11.064 --> 00:50:12.935
Look, grandfather.

00:50:12.955 --> 00:50:16.388
He likes me, says William.

00:50:16.448 --> 00:50:18.230
Do you like him?

00:50:18.290 --> 00:50:20.051
asks the grandfather.

00:50:20.111 --> 00:50:23.413
Yes, I like him a lot.

00:50:23.473 --> 00:50:26.094
Says the young boy, happily.

00:50:26.154 --> 00:50:30.136
The grandfather looks at my teeth and my legs.

00:50:30.196 --> 00:50:34.148
Well, I'm buying him for you, William.

00:50:34.208 --> 00:50:36.100
Says the grandfather.

00:50:36.160 --> 00:50:38.451
You must look after him.

00:50:38.511 --> 00:50:42.564
You must feed him and groom him every day.

00:50:42.624 --> 00:50:45.036
You can make him feel better.

00:50:45.096 --> 00:50:47.697
He is your responsibility.

00:50:47.758 --> 00:50:50.810
Oh, thank you, grandfather.

00:50:50.870 --> 00:50:53.405
Says William, kissing him.

00:50:53.465 --> 00:50:57.272
I promise to look after him.

00:50:57.332 --> 00:51:01.986
William and Mr. Turner, take me to their stables.

00:51:02.046 --> 00:51:08.222
I have a big, clean stall with lots of oats and fresh water.

00:51:08.282 --> 00:51:14.686
There is a small meadow outside where I can eat grass and enjoy the sun.

00:51:14.746 --> 00:51:18.520
Young William is a perfect master.

00:51:18.580 --> 00:51:22.585
Now you must wrasse beauty, says William.

00:51:22.645 --> 00:51:28.109
Soon you can run in the meadow with the other horses.

00:51:28.169 --> 00:51:33.761
Mr. Turner works on the farm and sometimes he comes to see me.

00:51:33.821 --> 00:51:36.892
He looks at my legs and my teeth.

00:51:36.952 --> 00:51:41.123
Then he talks to me and gives me some sugar.

00:51:41.183 --> 00:51:44.144
Black beauty is feeling better.

00:51:44.204 --> 00:51:46.425
Says Mr. Turner to William.

00:51:46.485 --> 00:51:49.710
His legs and knees are strong now.

00:51:49.770 --> 00:51:53.396
You're doing a good job with this horse.

00:51:53.456 --> 00:51:58.558
William smiles and says, thank you, grandfather.

00:51:58.618 --> 00:52:01.370
I love black beauty.

00:52:01.430 --> 00:52:02.850
I do too.

00:52:02.910 --> 00:52:04.371
Says Mr. Turner.

00:52:04.431 --> 00:52:07.162
He's a wonderful horse.

00:52:07.222 --> 00:52:15.468
The Bloamfield sisters are friends of Mr. Turner, and they are looking for a good horse.

00:52:15.528 --> 00:52:20.615
Black Beauty is feeling fine now, says Mr Turner.

00:52:20.675 --> 00:52:26.028
Let's take him to the Bloomfield sisters and see what they say.

00:52:26.088 --> 00:52:29.240
Yes, grandfather, says William.

00:52:29.301 --> 00:52:32.552
What a good idea.

00:52:32.612 --> 00:52:39.436
One summer day, William and Mr Turner take me to visit their friends.

00:52:39.496 --> 00:52:44.812
Ellen Bloomfield and her two sisters are happy when they see me.

00:52:44.872 --> 00:52:49.565
This horse has a good face, and he's very handsome.

00:52:49.625 --> 00:52:50.935
Says Ellen.

00:52:50.995 --> 00:52:52.556
I like him.

00:52:52.616 --> 00:52:54.787
Can I try him for a week?

00:52:54.847 --> 00:52:56.428
Yes, of course.

00:52:56.488 --> 00:52:59.208
Says Mr Turner, happily.

00:52:59.268 --> 00:53:05.422
A stable boy takes me to a big stable and starts grooming me.

00:53:05.482 --> 00:53:12.044
Every morning he comes to my store and pats me and talks to me.

00:53:12.104 --> 00:53:14.518
Good morning, Beauty.

00:53:14.578 --> 00:53:18.211
He says, what a lovely day!

00:53:18.271 --> 00:53:21.872
You can go to the meadow today!

00:53:21.932 --> 00:53:26.063
He grooms me and gives me an apple.

00:53:26.123 --> 00:53:29.244
Then he takes me to the meadow.

00:53:29.304 --> 00:53:34.616
I like the tall trees and the beautiful flowers.

00:53:34.676 --> 00:53:38.166
I feel better every day.

00:53:38.226 --> 00:53:42.598
This is the same star black beauty has.

00:53:42.658 --> 00:53:47.888
says the young man, looking at the white star on my face.

00:53:47.948 --> 00:53:53.179
And this is the same white foot too.

00:53:53.239 --> 00:53:59.270
He looks at my back and sees a little white spot.

00:53:59.330 --> 00:54:05.291
Oh, this is black beauty, he cries.

00:54:05.351 --> 00:54:09.472
Black beauty, do you remember me?

00:54:09.532 --> 00:54:11.751
I'm Joe Green.

00:54:11.811 --> 00:54:15.772
The stable boy at Mr. Gordon's!

00:54:15.832 --> 00:54:19.622
I put my nose in his hand.

00:54:19.682 --> 00:54:23.724
Yes, it is Joe Green.

00:54:23.784 --> 00:54:29.386
He is very happy and tells the Blomfield sisters about me.

00:54:29.446 --> 00:54:34.587
They are happy too and they want to keep me forever.

00:54:34.648 --> 00:54:38.857
Now I am part of the Blomfield family.

00:54:38.917 --> 00:54:45.117
Ellen writes me almost every day and I am her favorite horse.

00:54:45.177 --> 00:54:50.208
Sometimes I take her sisters to town in the carriage.

00:54:50.268 --> 00:54:56.610
My good friends, Mr. Turner and William, often come to visit me.

00:54:56.670 --> 00:55:09.352
I am finally happy in this wonderful home because everyone loves me and I love them.

00:55:09.412 --> 00:55:14.392
Listening activity.

00:55:14.452 --> 00:55:19.524
Ellen and Mr. Turner meet at the bakers.

00:55:19.584 --> 00:55:24.446
Ellen is buying biscuits and a chocolate cake.

00:55:24.507 --> 00:55:27.228
Hello Mr. Turner.

00:55:27.288 --> 00:55:28.958
It's good to see you.

00:55:28.978 --> 00:55:30.849
Hello Ellen.

00:55:30.909 --> 00:55:33.200
Nice to see you too.

00:55:33.260 --> 00:55:36.231
Are you looking for a good horse?

00:55:36.291 --> 00:55:37.512
Yes.

00:55:37.572 --> 00:55:40.588
I'm looking for a gentle horse.

00:55:40.648 --> 00:55:44.014
I have a wonderful horse for you.

00:55:44.074 --> 00:55:49.258
His name is Black Beauty and he's five years old.

00:55:49.318 --> 00:55:54.062
He's very gentle and he's perfect for a lady.

00:55:54.122 --> 00:55:56.544
When can I see him?

00:55:56.604 --> 00:56:01.648
I can bring him to your house next week on Tuesday.

00:56:01.708 --> 00:56:03.509
That's good.

00:56:03.569 --> 00:56:06.371
Come in the morning before lunch.

00:56:06.431 --> 00:56:08.364
Where do you live?

00:56:08.424 --> 00:56:12.990
I live in the big white house near the river.

00:56:13.050 --> 00:56:16.404
How much does the horse cost?

00:56:16.464 --> 00:56:29.642
I can sell him to you for 18 pounds.

00:56:29.702 --> 00:56:39.998
Oh.

